177
00:58:58,840 --> 00:58:59,180
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you.

178
00:59:01,130 --> 00:59:05,590
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Hanggang kailan po kayo naglingkod sa Office of the Solicitor General?

179
00:59:06,330 --> 00:59:11,130
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: I served the Office of the Solicitor General for almost 31 years.

180
00:59:11,900 --> 00:59:23,180
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Wow. 31 years. Estimate lang po, sa loob ng 31 years na yan, baka mahihirapan po kayo. Pero mga ilang kaso ang nahawakan ninyo sa OSG?

181
00:59:24,360 --> 00:59:27,360
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: More than a thousand cases, maybe.

182
00:59:27,900 --> 00:59:32,980
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Bakit po hanggang 2012 lang kayo naglingkod sa Office of the Solicitor General?

183
00:59:33,540 --> 00:59:38,480
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: I was appointed as Associate Justice of the Sandigan Bayan.

184
00:59:39,250 --> 00:59:47,710
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sa Supreme Court po meron mga justice, associate justice at meron din isang chief justice. Sa Sandigan Bayan po ba ganun din?

185
00:59:48,070 --> 00:59:52,120
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Wala po. Ang meron sa amin ay presiding justice.

186
00:59:52,720 --> 00:59:59,980
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Para po sa kaalaman ng lahat, ano po yung pagkaiba ng justice ng Sandigan Bayan at presiding justice?

187
01:00:01,380 --> 01:00:17,940
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ang presiding justice ay ang tinatawag na primus inter pares, the first among equals. Pero in terms of formal rank, pare-pareho naman kami, except that the presiding justice does some administrative work and leads the court.

188
01:00:25,020 --> 01:00:31,940
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Mayroon pa ba kayong na-appoint din po ba kayo sa yung sinasabi po ninyong first among equals?

189
01:00:33,180 --> 01:00:34,080
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

190
01:00:34,860 --> 01:00:39,100
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Kailan po kayo na-appoint bilang presiding justice ng Sandigan Bayan?

191
01:00:39,360 --> 01:00:39,920
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: 2013.

192
01:00:40,720 --> 01:00:43,580
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: At hanggang kailan po kayo naglingkod bilang PJ?

193
01:00:44,060 --> 01:00:46,560
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Until November 8, 2024.

194
01:00:47,580 --> 01:00:51,760
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Why was it only until 2024 that you served in the court?

195
01:00:52,860 --> 01:00:54,160
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: I retired, sir.

196
01:00:55,460 --> 01:01:09,660
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sa madaling salita po, Justice, you devoted your entire career as a lawyer from 1980 up to your retirement in 2024. That is 44 years to public service as a legal professional. Would that be a fair statement?

197
01:01:10,100 --> 01:01:10,660
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Tama po.

198
01:01:11,320 --> 01:01:20,200
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sana po all. Sana maraming abogado ang tumulad sa inyo. Asensya po, Your Honors, hindi po ako makapigil. Kayo po ba ay nagtuturo ng law?

199
01:01:21,190 --> 01:01:28,550
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. I teach law in the San Beda. University as well as the University of Santo Tomas.

200
01:01:28,650 --> 01:01:32,330
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ano pong subject o subjects ang itinuturo ninyo sa law?

201
01:01:32,790 --> 01:01:43,410
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: I teach Criminal Law 1 and 2 and Criminal Law Review in the San Pedro College of Law. And I teach Criminal Law 1 and 2 at the University of Santo Tomas.

202
01:01:44,170 --> 01:02:00,400
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Kasama po ba sa Criminal Law yung mga batas laban sa korupsyon tulad ng Republic Act? 3019, Republic Act 1379, Republic Act 6713, Code of Responsive Conduct of Government Officials.

203
01:02:00,640 --> 01:02:01,400
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

204
01:02:02,320 --> 01:02:09,880
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: At ano naman po yung naging involvement ninyo kung meron man sa mga nakaraang bar examinations?

205
01:02:10,780 --> 01:02:17,480
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, I was a bar examiner in 2015 and also last 2025 in political law.

206
01:02:17,760 --> 01:02:27,290
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Hindi po lahat ng tao ay nakaka... Ang maalam kung ano yung ginagawa ng isang bar examiner. Pwede po ninyong pakipaliwanag po yan?

207
01:02:27,750 --> 01:02:50,400
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, a bar examiner, if chosen by the bar chairperson in the Supreme Court, is asked to submit questions to the bar chairperson. And we check actually the test papers, not the answers, it's now online, of the bar examinees.

208
01:02:50,980 --> 01:02:58,960
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sabi po ninyo, naglingkod kayo bilang bar examiner noong 2015 at 2025. Ano pong subject sa mga bar subjects?

209
01:02:59,500 --> 01:03:00,480
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Political law po.

210
01:03:00,920 --> 01:03:07,200
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Political law. Kasama po ba sa political law yung constitutional law, yung ating 1987 Constitution?

211
01:03:07,740 --> 01:03:08,380
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

212
01:03:08,790 --> 01:03:17,480
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: At yung po bang mga provision ng Constitution, halimbawa tungkol sa public accountability ay kasama po rin po yun, sakop po yun?

213
01:03:17,680 --> 01:03:18,260
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

214
01:03:18,320 --> 01:03:19,000
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you.

215
01:03:20,910 --> 01:03:35,450
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Move on. Well, balikan ko po ng konti yung inyong paglilingkod nung nasa Office of the Solicitor General po kayo. May experience po ba kayo noong nasa OSG kayo sa mga kasong unexplained or ill-gotten wealth?

216
01:03:36,120 --> 01:03:44,470
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. I handled, among other lawyers in the Office of the Solicitor General, the so-called ill-gotten wealth cases.

217
01:03:45,300 --> 01:03:49,940
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: In what capacity did you handle those ill-gotten wealth cases, Justice?

218
01:03:51,760 --> 01:04:11,480
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: As a solicitor, I handle those cases but when PCGG chairman Sabio took the helm of the PCGG, he created a PCGG-OSG task force where I was designated as the chairperson of the task force.

219
01:04:12,020 --> 01:04:18,200
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Bilang chairperson po ng PCGG-OSG task force. Ano-ano po yung ginagawa ninyo?

220
01:04:18,440 --> 01:04:20,520
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. May we know the relevance, Your Honor.

221
01:04:21,040 --> 01:04:23,200
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Establishing qualifications, if Your Honor is pleased.

222
01:04:24,080 --> 01:04:25,360
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Overruled. Witness may answer.

223
01:04:26,560 --> 01:04:35,700
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: I reviewed the pleadings of The cases related to those cases.

224
01:04:36,100 --> 01:04:48,920
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Estimate lang po, mga ilang oras ang inilaan ninyo sa mga kasong ill-gotten wealth na nabanggit ninyo bilang solicitor at later bilang chairperson ng task force? Estimate lang po.

225
01:04:49,630 --> 01:04:53,110
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Probably thousand of hours po.

226
01:04:56,530 --> 01:05:02,970
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sunod pong tanong, how about civil forfeiture cases involving money laundering? Nakahawag din po kayo ng ganun?

227
01:05:03,110 --> 01:05:14,670
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes sir, because the OSG actually is lawyer or acts as a lawyer and files actually these petitions for civil forfeiture with appropriate court.

228
01:05:14,990 --> 01:05:22,800
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So nung time po na yun... And that is the situation, isn't it, that the OSJ may hold? Yes. Let's

229
01:05:22,800 --> 01:05:35,780
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: go back to the time when you were the justice and presiding justice of Sandigan Bayan. What is the difference between Sandigan Bayan and other courts? What is unique about it?

230
01:05:36,680 --> 01:06:03,080
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, the Sandigan Bayan is a unique court simply because it is both a trial court and appellate court. Pero siyang original jurisdiction and appellate court at the same time. And it is a special court because it tries mostly criminal cases involving high government officials and even private individuals actually who are alleged to have conspired with them in the commission of these crimes.

231
01:06:05,140 --> 01:06:28,020
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: More or less lang po, again, just an estimate for the benefit of the court and the public. How many cases more or less did you hear involving the application of Republic Act 3019, the Anti-Graft and Corrupt Practices Act, Civil Forfeiture of Unexplained Wealth under Republic Act 1379, and the Code of Conduct of Public Officials and Employees under Republic Act 6713?

232
01:06:29,930 --> 01:06:33,950
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: All in all, probably around 700 cases, sir.

233
01:06:35,220 --> 01:06:45,600
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: That must have taken you a lot of time po to hear and decide those cases? Mga ilang oras kaya ang inilaan ninyo Para sa pagdinig at pagdesisyon ng mga kasong iyon?

234
01:06:47,490 --> 01:06:50,390
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Probably mga thousands of hours din po.

235
01:06:51,200 --> 01:07:07,060
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Just to, kung susumahin lang po natin, sa loob ng 42 years na kayo ay lingkot bayan, how many hours of that did you spend in terms of studying and analyzing cases of anti-corruption?

236
01:07:10,560 --> 01:07:13,040
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Baka mahigit 5,000 hours or more.

237
01:07:13,360 --> 01:07:32,870
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you, thank you po Justice. I hope, Your Honor, the defense will not object to my next question kahit may pagka maritest po siya. Ito naman po ay para sa mga law student na nangangarap maglingkod bilang maestrado. Nung nasa OSG po kayo, sino po yung mga nakasabay ninyo na later na-appoint sa judiciary?

238
01:07:34,250 --> 01:07:53,740
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Marami po. Dalawang nasa Supreme Court ngayon. Yung isang presiding justice ng Court of Appeals, Court of Tax Appeals. Yung nag-retire din ng Court of Tax Appeals presiding justice. At sa Sandigan Bayan, may mga incumbents din po akong mga nakasama nun sa OSG.

239
01:07:54,570 --> 01:08:01,230
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: If your honor, please, I have finished questioning the witness on her qualifications. May I proceed to the substance of her testimony?

240
01:08:02,890 --> 01:08:03,930
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed, counsel.

241
01:08:04,150 --> 01:08:08,950
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you, your honor. Okay, panaman po kayo. Please have some water if you need to.

242
01:08:12,660 --> 01:08:33,640
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Justice Tang, lagi po natin naririnig yung mga salitang unexplained wealth, hidden wealth, ill-gotten wealth. Para sa mga ordinaryong Pilipino, parang magkapareho lang naman ng mga terms na yan. Sa mata po ng batas, may pagkakaiba po ba yung hidden wealth, unexplained wealth, at ill-gotten wealth?

243
01:08:34,160 --> 01:08:37,480
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: May pagkakaiba po sila.

244
01:08:38,080 --> 01:08:39,520
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ano po yung pagkakaiba?

245
01:08:39,860 --> 01:09:21,480
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, ang hidden wealth. simply means tagong yaman. Ang unexplained wealth naman, this is governed by RA 1379 in relation to RA 3019. Ang ill-gotten wealth naman ay governed by EO numbers 1, 2, 14. Makikita mo rin ito sa transitory provisions of the 1987 Constitution. At yung definition niyan ay matatagpuan rin sa Section 1D ng Republic Act No. 7080 or the Plunder Law as amended.

246
01:09:21,920 --> 01:09:33,300
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So kapag binigyan po ang isang lingkod bayan, let's say lang po ha, ng isang bribe, let's say ng 50 million pesos at tinago niya sa pangalan ng ibang tao, hidden wealth po yun.

247
01:09:33,380 --> 01:09:33,960
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor.

248
01:09:34,000 --> 01:09:34,560
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Speculative.

249
01:09:35,680 --> 01:09:37,420
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Um, what if I counsel?

250
01:09:38,590 --> 01:09:39,930
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: May I respond? I know where

251
01:09:39,930 --> 01:09:40,470
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you're getting it.

252
01:09:41,030 --> 01:09:48,150
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your Honor. Maari po ba kayo magbigay ng halimbawa ng hidden wealth na sinasabi niyong tagong yaman?

253
01:09:49,620 --> 01:10:01,950
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: For example, a public officer owns, actually owns a property but that property is registered in the name of another person.

254
01:10:03,070 --> 01:10:05,230
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yun po ang nakatagong yaman? Yes.

255
01:10:05,270 --> 01:10:05,730
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

256
01:10:06,070 --> 01:10:09,910
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Maari po ba kayo magbigay ng isang halimbawa ng unexplained wealth?

257
01:10:11,220 --> 01:10:18,810
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Unexplained wealth is actually defined in Section 2 of RA 1379.

258
01:10:22,220 --> 01:10:30,480
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Babalikan po natin yung puntong yan mamaya-maya. Huling tunang po on this point lang. How about an example for ill-gotten wealth?

259
01:10:31,590 --> 01:10:34,810
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ill-gotten wealth according to EO No. 1

260
01:10:36,320 --> 01:10:49,550
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ayun ay mga kayamanan or yaman that was acquired through illegal means like through bribery, misappropriation, malversation, and the like.

261
01:10:49,850 --> 01:10:58,670
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you, Justice. Ipakita po natin, request lang po sa tech booth, sa screen ang Section 8 ng Republic Act 3019.

262
01:11:00,500 --> 01:11:22,360
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Kita po ninyo, Justice, napakahaba niyan tapos puro English na mahirap intindihin. It's very hard even just to read this. Mga bigatin po na salita sa Ingles pa ang ginagamit at nakakaalam mga abugado. Pwede po natin gawin simple ito. Kailan nagiging questionable sa ilalim ng batas ang yaman ng isang opisyal?

263
01:11:24,020 --> 01:11:43,680
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ayon sa batas, ito'y questionable if during the incumbency of the public official, he acquired wealth that is grossly disproportionate. To his salary, other lawful income and income generated from his legitimately acquired property.

264
01:12:05,820 --> 01:12:09,660
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Tutuong kayamanan dun sa kanyang lehitimong kita. Tama po yun?

265
01:12:09,800 --> 01:12:10,160
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes.

266
01:12:11,540 --> 01:12:17,360
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Paano malalaman ng pamahalaan kung ang isang opisyal ay meron ng unexplained wealth?

267
01:12:18,400 --> 01:12:26,000
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ito'y karaniwan malalaman kung ang isang opisyal ay nagsumiti ng true and accurate sell-in.

268
01:12:27,360 --> 01:12:39,800
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ah, dun pa pala nakikita. Thank you for that justice. Ano-ano mga bagay naman ang dapat tingnan? ng mga nag-iimbestiga ng unexplained wealth maliban po sa SAL-N.

269
01:12:41,520 --> 01:12:46,400
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yung lifestyle, IT, yung income tax returns.

270
01:12:47,830 --> 01:13:20,670
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: How about the records, for example, pertaining to the financial status of that person? Objection, leading. Can you modify, counsel? If you're honest, please, the question is not leading, it's how about. I'm asking the witness. But anyway, I will replace. Can you modify, counsel? Yes, thank you. Nabanggit po ninyo kanina na tinitingnan po ninyo yung SAL-N, tinitingnan po ninyo yung ITR. What other records, if any, does an investigator look at when it comes to unexplained wealth?

271
01:13:21,270 --> 01:13:29,330
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Even the properties and assets of the spouse and the children under 18 years of age.

272
01:13:29,670 --> 01:14:04,240
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, sorry to interrupt. Yes, Attorney Mark. Just a query, Your Honor. Actually, this is the danger that we were concerned about because I don't think the prosecution qualified this witness as an expert witness. Therefore, whatever opinion that she will share with us today is not expert opinion but just her personal opinion. And that is the danger of presenting her because she might present her own interpretations of the law, again, which is the function of this court, Your Honor.

273
01:14:05,770 --> 01:14:08,590
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: So we're objecting to this line of questions.

274
01:14:09,110 --> 01:14:24,150
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Again, counsel, whatever she says is subject to cross her representation of another witness. Besides, anything she says, as the court said, as the presiding officer said earlier, is neither conclusive nor binding upon this court.

275
01:14:25,720 --> 01:14:39,260
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, we will note the objection. The objection is overruled and you have a continuing objection with respect to this witness's qualification anyway. Attorney, rather Honorable Chell, you may proceed.

276
01:14:39,600 --> 01:15:32,950
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you, Your Honor. Ipakita po natin sa screen ang bahagi ng Section 8 na nakahighlight. Ayan po. Focus po muna tayo dun sa unang bahagi ng Section 8. Kasi medyo mahirap lunokin yung buong provision po na yan at napakahaba. I'll just read it if I may. Quote, If in accordance with the provisions of Republic Act 1379, a public official has been found to have acquired during his incumbency, whether in his name or in the name of other persons, an amount of property and or money manifestly out of proportion to his salary, and to his other lawful income, that fact shall be a ground for dismissal or removal. I'd like to emphasis the last part, yung pong nakalagay na that fact shall be a ground for dismissal or removal. Ano pong ibig sabihin ito?

277
01:15:33,710 --> 01:15:51,890
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ang ibig niyang sabihin ay if a public officer is found to have acquired unexplained wealth, In accordance with Republic Act 1379, that is a ground for removal or dismissal.

278
01:15:52,740 --> 01:16:05,260
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sa madaling salita po, pagka napatunayan nga yung mga kinakailangan ng batas para sa masabi na merong unexplained wealth, ito ay maaaring nang tanggalin ang opisyal na iyon.

279
01:16:05,400 --> 01:16:06,060
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

280
01:16:06,320 --> 01:16:54,620
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Balikan po natin ang Section 8 ng... RA 3019. Babalikan po natin mamaya yung Section 8. Punta po muna tayo sa Section 2 ng RA1379. Ayan po yung nasa screen po ngayon. Nakalagay naman dito, quote, Whenever any public officer or employee has acquired during his incumbency an amount of property which is manifestly out of proportion to his salary, a such public officer or employee, and to his other lawful income and the income from legitimately acquired property, said property shall be presumed prima facie to have been unlawfully acquired Palagay ko po yung salitang presumed prima facie ay medyo mahirap intindihin. Sa simpleng salita, maaari po ba ninyong ipaliwanag po yun?

281
01:16:56,360 --> 01:17:28,800
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ang ibig sabihin po ng prima facie, actually prima facie is a Latin word. It means, literally in English, on the face of it or on its face. So ang ibig sabihin yan, kapag napakita ng isang opisyal ay nag-acquire ng property that is grossly or manifestly disproportionate to his salary, lawful income, and income from lawfully acquired properties, ito ay ipinapalagay na unlawfully acquired.

282
01:17:29,660 --> 01:17:35,960
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ilinawin po natin, kapag may ganitong presumption, ibig bang sabihin ay guilty na agad ang opisyal?

283
01:17:36,160 --> 01:17:58,420
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ay hindi po. Itong presumption na ito ay rebuttable. Ibig sabihin kapag magkapag... Presenta ng ebidensya naman or maipaliwanag satisfactorily ng empleyado or opisyal that he acquired those properties lawfully, mawawala po yung visa ng presumption na yan.

284
01:17:59,490 --> 01:18:10,550
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you so much, Justice. In other words, Justice, kung hindi tugma ang yaman ng isang opisyal sa kanyang legal na kita, pwedeng itanong na ng batas saan ang galing ang pera?

285
01:18:10,810 --> 01:18:11,730
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

286
01:18:12,780 --> 01:18:22,920
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: At siyempre, may obligasyon po ba? I will withdraw and ask another question. At may obligasyon po ba ang pamahalaan na imbestigahan nito?

287
01:18:23,120 --> 01:18:24,480
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Rejection leading, Your Honor.

288
01:18:25,200 --> 01:18:30,220
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I will rephrase. What obligation does the government have in that situation?

289
01:18:30,920 --> 01:18:38,500
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, Section 8 of RA 1379 mandates that a preliminary inquiry be conducted.

290
01:18:39,870 --> 01:18:44,080
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Move on na po tayo, Justice, sa pangalawang paksa.

291
01:18:45,900 --> 01:18:54,140
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Justice, paano naman kung sabihin ng isang opisyal, eh hindi naman sa akin nakapangalan niyang property. Tapos na po ba agad ang

292
01:18:54,140 --> 01:18:55,840
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: usapan? Objection speculative, Your Honor.

293
01:18:58,110 --> 01:19:00,510
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Candidate Forum Counsel, again, you know how to get there.

294
01:19:02,110 --> 01:19:11,590
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Justice Tang, what is the state of the law when it comes to property that is in the name of a person other than the government official concerned?

295
01:19:12,710 --> 01:19:36,520
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, under Section 8 of Republic Act 3019, the properties in the name of other persons and even the spouse and the children may be considered in determining whether the official has unlawfully accord. Properties.

296
01:19:36,520 --> 01:19:43,360
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Bakit po? Bakit pati ang ari-arian ng asawa at ng ibang tao ay maaari din tingnan sa ilalim ng batas?

297
01:19:43,500 --> 01:19:45,720
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection already calls for an opinion, Your Honor.

298
01:19:46,360 --> 01:19:55,980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: He qualified, he tried to at least qualify the witness as an expert counsel. Again, for as long as it is general and does not apply specifically to this case, we will allow it. Your

299
01:19:55,980 --> 01:20:02,580
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Honor, can we just make a clarification? Was she qualified as a legal expert by the court? No, the

300
01:20:02,580 --> 01:20:26,260
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: court need not declare a witness to be an expert, counsel. Again, as the court said earlier, subject to cross and subject to using the factors in the Frye and Dobert case. You may question this witness's credibility, reliability, and expertise, if any. Again, whatever she says will not be binding nor conclusive upon the court anyway.

301
01:20:27,010 --> 01:20:27,890
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: We'll submit your

302
01:20:27,890 --> 01:20:30,610
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: order. Honorable Chal, you may proceed.

303
01:20:32,580 --> 01:20:33,120
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sir,

304
01:20:33,260 --> 01:20:34,680
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: can you please repeat the question?

305
01:20:36,340 --> 01:20:47,140
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Bakit po pagdating po sa bagay ng unexplained wealth ay pati yung mga ari-arian ng asawa o mga nakapangalan sa ibang tao ay maaari din tingnan?

306
01:20:47,920 --> 01:21:13,290
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, according to the Supreme Court, actually in the case of Republic v. Rabusa and Rabusa v. Republic, this is to prevent concealment. and to obviate the circumstance that a public official is able to evade investigation.

307
01:21:14,220 --> 01:21:29,220
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you, Justice. Ipakita po natin yung Section 8 ng Republic Act 3019 na nakahighlight po yung susunod na slide, please. Next slide, please.

308
01:21:30,860 --> 01:22:06,520
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Meron pong nakahighlight dyan sa bandang gitna ng Section 8. Pabasahin ko lang po yung bahagi na iyon. Bank deposits in the name of the public official, his spouse or any of their dependents shall likewise be taken into consideration in the enforcement of this section, notwithstanding any provision of law to the contrary. Paliwanag na po ninyo yung maaring natingnan ng properties ng asawa o mga dependent. Pero ano po yung nakalagay doon sa dulo? Notwithstanding any provision of law to the contrary.

309
01:22:07,140 --> 01:22:14,160
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ang ibig sabihin po yan ay kahit may nagbabawal na batas na gawin yun.

310
01:22:14,960 --> 01:22:18,940
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Move on na po tayo sa pangatlong paksa.

311
01:22:22,310 --> 01:22:33,440
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Justice, punta naman tayo sa presidente at vicepresidente. Pareho lang po ba ang rules? Sa kanila at sa ordinaryong government employee pagdating sa kanilang kita at financial interests?

312
01:22:33,560 --> 01:22:34,680
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection leading, Your Honor.

313
01:22:35,660 --> 01:22:48,040
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: May I respond if Your Honor is pleased? Yes, Honorable Shell. Can I respond? I am simply asking if the rules are the same. But if the court would like, I can rephrase the question to make it non-leading.

314
01:22:48,400 --> 01:22:53,880
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly rephrase, counsel, but in the interest of time as well.

315
01:22:54,240 --> 01:23:03,650
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: What are the rules, Justice, insofar as a President and Vice President are concerned as compared to the ordinary government employee.

316
01:23:04,470 --> 01:23:14,510
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: There are stricter prohibitions on the President and Vice President and even actually the Cabinet Secretaries. They're under secretaries and assistants.

317
01:23:15,330 --> 01:23:20,950
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Bakit po mas mahigpit ang batas pagdating sa Presidente, Vice Presidente at Cabinet members?

318
01:23:22,370 --> 01:23:28,860
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, ayon sa Korte Suprema in the case of Civil Liberties Union, versus Executive Secretary.

319
01:23:30,510 --> 01:23:35,570
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: There is the greater possibility of abuse in their office given their positions.

320
01:23:36,590 --> 01:23:48,690
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, please. If I may be allowed to make a manifestation. Your Honor, we understand the position of this court that the testimony of the witness is not binding upon this court. But how about the general public?

321
01:23:50,910 --> 01:24:06,750
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: This already serves as conditioning of the mind of the public. After all, the public is not educated as to which of these laws that the witness is testifying on is applicable to this case or not. And we just want to make that for the record.

322
01:24:25,450 --> 01:24:49,280
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: To the facts surrounding this case and this case in particular against the respondent. But the prosecution wishes to use up one of their 15 witnesses and one of their trial dates on the Honorable Justice Tang. And the court allowed it, counsel. So you may proceed, Honorable Jackdo.

323
01:24:49,710 --> 01:24:55,990
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you, Your Honor. Ipakita po natin ang Article 7, Section 6 ng ating Constitution, please.

324
01:24:59,110 --> 01:25:21,170
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Meron pong nakasulat po sa bandang dulo nitong provision. First, in the beginning part of this provision, it says, the salaries of the President and Vice President shall be determined by law. And then at the end, it says, they shall not receive during their tenure any other emolument from the government or any other source. Ano pong ibig sabihin ito?

325
01:25:22,250 --> 01:25:33,710
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Simply, ang ibig sabihin niyan, hindi pwedeng tumanggap yung presidente o vicepresidente ng sahod mula sa kanilang legitimate na sahod at sa iba pang sources.

326
01:25:34,430 --> 01:25:43,850
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Eh kami pong mga mambabatas ay wala naman pong ganun na restriction. Bakit po ganitong kahigpit ang konstitusyon natin pagdating sa pangulo at pangalawang pangulo?

327
01:25:44,090 --> 01:25:59,930
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, it's the same reason I gave in the case of, cited by the Supreme Court in the case of Civil Society versus Executive Secretary.

328
01:26:00,410 --> 01:26:04,790
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you po. Move on na po tayo sa pang-apat na paksa.

329
01:26:07,460 --> 01:26:11,680
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Habang po ay presidente o vice-presidente ang isang tawag...

330
01:26:11,680 --> 01:26:21,620
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: With the permission of the Honorable Jocno, Justice Tang, you interpreted emolument to mean salary? If I heard you correctly?

331
01:26:21,940 --> 01:26:22,340
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

332
01:26:22,540 --> 01:26:23,220
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Okay. Thank

333
01:26:23,220 --> 01:26:23,360
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: you.

334
01:26:24,460 --> 01:26:26,500
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: If I may proceed, Your Honor.

335
01:26:26,800 --> 01:26:27,400
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: If

336
01:26:30,370 --> 01:26:31,490
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I may proceed, Your Honor, please.

337
01:26:33,130 --> 01:26:41,890
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Question po, Justice. Habang presidente o vicepresidente, pwede po ba silang basta sumali o makilahok sa negosyo?

338
01:26:42,130 --> 01:26:42,990
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Hindi po.

339
01:26:43,810 --> 01:26:47,410
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Saan pong batas nakalagay ang pagbabawal na ito?

340
01:26:48,270 --> 01:26:52,570
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: I think it's Section 13 of Article 7 of the Constitution.

341
01:26:53,610 --> 01:26:57,530
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ipakita po natin ang Section 13. Yes.

342
01:26:59,770 --> 01:27:12,070
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Madali lang po naman naiintindihin yung ibang salita dyan. They cannot directly participate in business. Pero ano po kaya ang ibig sabihin ng indirectly na mag-participate na bawal daw?

343
01:27:13,740 --> 01:27:22,100
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Indirectly simply means hindi silang gumagawa pero iba ang gumagawa but in their name. So ibang tao ang gumagawa para sa kanila.

344
01:27:23,100 --> 01:27:25,660
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sa ganun sitwasyon, sino pong nakikinabang?

345
01:27:28,380 --> 01:27:29,080
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yung official.

346
01:27:30,390 --> 01:27:35,550
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Dito po ba pumapasok yung salitang beneficial owner?

347
01:27:36,910 --> 01:27:37,870
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

348
01:27:38,610 --> 01:27:45,650
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Siyempre po maraming mga kababayan natin ay hindi po pamilyarang sa salitang beneficial owner. Pakipaliwanag po.

349
01:27:46,070 --> 01:28:03,050
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ang beneficial owner ay yung tunay na taong nagmamayari ng ari-arian. or sa interest sa korporasyon. Although, based on legal documents, ibang taong nakapangalan doon.

350
01:28:04,680 --> 01:28:15,260
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you so much, Justice. One more question on this point. So, ibig sabihin, posibleng magkaiba ang pangalan na nasa papel at ang taong tunay na nakikinabang o may financial interest?

351
01:28:15,620 --> 01:28:16,320
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

352
01:28:16,620 --> 01:28:20,140
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Move on na po tayo sa panglimang paksa.

353
01:28:23,110 --> 01:28:29,430
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Justice, may isa pang sinasabi ang ating konstitusyon na pwede pong ipakita ang Article 7, Section 13.

354
01:28:31,470 --> 01:28:42,830
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Nakalagay po dyan na bawal ang presidente at vicepresidente magkaroon ng financial interest sa kontrata, franchise, o special privilege mula sa gobyerno. Bakit po ganon?

355
01:28:43,850 --> 01:28:50,460
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Again, the ruling of the Supreme Court in the case of a civil

356
01:28:52,710 --> 01:28:53,670
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Liberties po.

357
01:28:53,910 --> 01:28:57,070
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Liberties versus executive secretary.

358
01:28:58,370 --> 01:29:08,790
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Maari po ba kayong magbigay ng halimbawa ng may financial interest sa kontrata ang isang presidente o vice-presidente?

359
01:29:09,590 --> 01:29:22,310
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, I will cite a case involving a Supreme Court case. The president entering into a contract of lease with a government agency.

360
01:29:23,820 --> 01:29:40,460
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So pagka ang Pangulo po ay nagkaroon ng kontrata kahit sabihin natin lease contract lahang po ay maaari po yan na maging paglabag sa having financial interest in a contract with the government.

361
01:29:40,840 --> 01:29:41,340
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes sir.

362
01:29:41,620 --> 01:30:00,100
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Meron pong nakalagay din sa bandang dulo nitong Section 13. They, this is referring to the President, Vice President and Cabinet members, quote, shall strictly avoid conflict of interest in the conduct of their office. Medyo mabigat pong salita yung conflict. Conflict

363
01:30:00,100 --> 01:30:01,620
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: of interest. Ano pong ibig sabihin nun?

364
01:30:02,410 --> 01:30:15,180
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Conflict of interest simply means na yung interest ng opisyal, pribadong interest ng opisyal na yun ay salungat sa interest ng pamahalaan ng kanyang pinagsisilbihan.

365
01:30:16,360 --> 01:30:38,150
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Salamat po. Move on na po tayo sa pinakahuling topic. Justice, napagusapan na natin yung legal nakita, napagusapan natin yung mga properties, negosyo, financial interest. Bilang public official, saan dapat i-deklara ang assets, liabilities, at net worth ng isang opisyal?

366
01:30:38,850 --> 01:30:48,070
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Sa kanyang SAL-N po. Statement of Assets, Liabilities, and Net Worth, Financial Interest, at saka Business Interest.

367
01:30:48,190 --> 01:30:54,090
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Para sa ordinaryong Pilipino po, bakit pa natin pinasa-SAL-N ang mga opisyal ng gobyerno?

368
01:30:54,740 --> 01:31:12,890
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ito ay nire-require hindi lang ng Constitution at iba pa nating ibang imuiral na batas para malaman kung ang isang opisyal ba ay umaman habang siya ay nasa pwesto at kung papaano niya na-acquire itong yaman na ito.

369
01:31:13,510 --> 01:31:17,230
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ipakita po natin ang first page ng sale and form please.

370
01:31:19,040 --> 01:31:27,460
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Para lang po ba itong form na basta-basta lang sinasubmit ng opisyal o may mas mahalagang layunin ito laban sa corruption?

371
01:31:28,590 --> 01:31:42,430
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, hindi lang ito basta-basta na form po. Ito ay kailangan isumite. And according to the Supreme Court, it must be true, correct, and proper form.

372
01:31:43,170 --> 01:31:48,370
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I-close up po natin yung gitnang bahagi po ng page 1 ng SAL-N, please.

373
01:31:50,550 --> 01:32:01,860
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Kung may asawa po ang public official, ano naman po ang kailangan i-disclose tungkol sa assets, liabilities? Business interests and financial connections ng kanyang asawa ayon sa batas.

374
01:32:02,240 --> 01:32:38,940
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ayon sa batas kailangan din isama yung mga ari-arian ng asawa. But let me just qualify sir. Because in the case of Abid Babano versus the Executive Secretary, ang sabi ng Korte Suprema, if the spouses had a complete separation of property, or sa property relations nila before the marriage, then the spouse of that official, the property of the spouse of the official need not be included in that official's SAL-N.

375
01:32:39,410 --> 01:32:56,030
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So, ibig sabihin po kapag meron yung tinatawag na prenuptial agreement ang magiging mag-asawa o kaya habang sila yung nag-asawa na ay nag-judicial separation of properties, hindi na po kailangan i-disclose sa SAL-N yung mga assets, liabilities, at net worth ng asawa.

376
01:32:56,190 --> 01:32:58,390
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. Yan po ang turo ng Supreme Court.

377
01:32:58,630 --> 01:33:04,470
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Ipakita po natin yung notarial acknowledgement po ng SAL-N form, please.

378
01:33:06,300 --> 01:33:13,160
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Justice, may isang bagay po na gusto ko lang itanong tungkol dito. Ang SAL-N po ba ay pinipirmahan under oath?

379
01:33:13,700 --> 01:33:15,660
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Opo, it's required under the law.

380
01:33:16,140 --> 01:33:28,220
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: At pakiclose up po yung notarial portion po ng SAL-N. E ano po ang ibig sabihin kapag ang isang dokumento tulad ng SAL-N ay pinirmahan na may pagpapanumpa?

381
01:33:29,820 --> 01:33:43,700
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well... Once a document is notarized, it becomes a public document. And everything that is stated there is attested to as truthful or true by the one who executes the document.

382
01:33:44,460 --> 01:33:50,020
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Malapit na po akong matapos. Ipakita po natin ang susunod po na slide.

383
01:33:52,440 --> 01:34:19,320
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sabi po ng Supreme Court sa isang desisyon, Office of the Ombudsman versus Valencia. And I will just quote that portion. A public officer in the discharge of duties is to use that prudence, caution, and attention which careful persons use in the management of his affairs. First question po, kasi medyo mabigat po itong mga salita. Ano pong ibig sabihin yan?

384
01:34:20,190 --> 01:34:28,670
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Dapat pag nag-submit ang isang official ng kanyang SAL-N, dapat ito ay tama at wasto?

385
01:34:30,050 --> 01:35:08,570
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ibig sabihin po, dapat maging maingat at prudente ang mga opisyal na ng ating gobyerno sa pag-fill up po at pag-execute ng SAL-N. Objection leading, Your Honor. I'll just move on if you're honest, please. Kindly move on, Counsel. Thank you. Huling slide na po, pakishow lang sa screen. In the same case, the Supreme Court said, and I quote, By the SAL-N, the public are able to monitor movement in the fortune of a public official. It is a valid check and balance mechanism to verify undisclosed properties and wealth. Ano pong masasabi niyo tungkol dyan sa pinasa ko?

386
01:35:09,740 --> 01:35:27,230
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ang ibig sabihin niyan ay ang SAL-N ay isang notoryadong dokumento and it is also an accountability framework para

387
01:35:28,990 --> 01:35:50,590
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: accountability framework. Kaya pag nag-execute ang isang official, dapat he should do it by exercising prudence, caution, and attention doon sa details na nakasaad doon sa kanyang statement of assets and liabilities.

388
01:35:51,170 --> 01:35:57,350
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I have no more questions. If Your Honor, please, I would just like to thank the good justice for her appearance today.

389
01:35:57,950 --> 01:36:02,770
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you. Will you cross today, Attorney Mark? Or do we proceed with the interjection of Senator-Judges?

390
01:36:03,030 --> 01:36:09,750
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, can we ask if we can be allowed to conduct our cross-examination after lunch?

391
01:36:10,880 --> 01:36:18,380
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: After lunch. After lunch it shall be. So we shall proceed with the interjections of Senator-Judges. Do we have a list, Anika?

392
01:36:19,000 --> 01:36:21,960
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Your Honor, may I be allowed to take my seat? Yes,

393
01:36:21,980 --> 01:36:24,380
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: of course, Attorney Chel. The Honorable Chel.

394
01:36:26,500 --> 01:36:35,980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Honorable Chel, forgive me if I confuse you. If I call you attorney sometimes, given that you're a member of Congress. May I get the list, Annika, please?

395
01:36:42,000 --> 01:36:42,400
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Okay,

396
01:36:50,770 --> 01:37:00,590
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: this is from Annika, not from me, okay? So if I didn't see your hands, it's not my fault. The Honorable Senator-Judge Rafi Tulfo is recognized for his interjection.

397
01:37:02,620 --> 01:37:04,780
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed when you're ready, sir. You have two minutes.

398
01:37:14,160 --> 01:37:26,660
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Madam Witness, yung bang labas-pasok na pera sa account ng isang public official at hindi po yan na-deklara sa SAL-N, ano po ang tawag doon?

399
01:37:28,190 --> 01:37:42,770
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, depende po yan kasi the SAL-N is required to be submitted every April 30 of the year. So, ang mag-govern dyan is magkano yung pera mo doon sa bank account mo at as of that time.

400
01:37:43,210 --> 01:38:05,630
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Halimbawa po umabot sa bilyones yung pasok-labas ng pera from a certain account ng isang public official, umabot na po ng bilyones and yet pag ibalance mo, bilyon pa rin po ang halaga total but it wasn't declared at sabihin na ayan ay pinark lang or ayan ay dumaan lang sa account ko at hindi ko naman talaga pera yan. How would you qualify that?

401
01:38:06,500 --> 01:38:20,090
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, still kap, basta nasa pangalan niya yung, nasa account name niya. o yung pangalan niya ang nandun sa account, that must still be declared in the SAL-N.

402
01:38:20,570 --> 01:38:23,350
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So kung hindi po na-declare sa SAL-N, ano pong tawag doon?

403
01:38:24,170 --> 01:38:25,570
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, it's an omission.

404
01:38:26,370 --> 01:38:36,770
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Omission. So would that be considered as unexplained wealth, hidden wealth, questionable wealth? Huwag po kayong gumamit ng RE. Kung gagamit kayo ng RE, pakidefine lang para maintindihan po yung taong bayan.

405
01:38:36,980 --> 01:39:04,320
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Hindi naman nangangahulugan na pag may omission doon sa SAL-N e kaagad sasabihin na there is unexplained wealth. Kasi according to the Supreme Court nga doon sa kaso ni Carlos versus Executive Secretary, dapat mabigyan ng pagkakataon iyong public officer na ipaliwanag bakit hindi na isama sa kanyang SAL-N iyong mga ibang assets na hindi naka-include doon sa kanyang SAL-N.

406
01:39:04,610 --> 01:39:11,970
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Pero kung perennial, palagi po nangyayari na lang, year after year, yung ganong klaseng omission na sinasabi niyo, so how would you consider that?

407
01:39:12,250 --> 01:39:31,630
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, according to the Supreme Court, dapat titignan mo kung yung omission na yan is an honest omission or it was an honest mistake vis-a-vis or compared to an intentional concealment. Pero that will already depend on the attending facts. Depende po yun.

408
01:39:31,990 --> 01:39:59,870
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. Halimbawa po, Maraming property ang isang public official at sabi nyo nga kanina kapag hindi dideklara that's unexplained wealth. Pero ang sasabihin naman ng isang public official eh yan naman ay sa aking husband at ang husband ko ay kumikita naman dahil siya ay merong magandang profesyon pero hindi na nadeclare ng husband although wala silang prenuptial agreement. How would you consider that?

409
01:40:03,590 --> 01:40:24,450
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Under RA 1379, binibigyan naman ng pagkakataon yung official na mag-explica o magpaliwanag. Kung katanggap-tanggap naman yung kanyang eksplanasyon na lawfully acquired yung properties na iyon, it will not be considered as unexplained wealth.

410
01:40:25,070 --> 01:40:33,020
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Lawfully acquired yung property na iyon pero it was not declared doon sa SAL-N. May problema ba doon o wala po, Madam Witness?

411
01:40:33,480 --> 01:40:51,730
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, according to the Supreme Court, again in the case of Carlos versus Executive Secretary, titignan maigi kung meron bang intentional omission yan or wala. O kaya intentional concealment that amounts to fraud.

412
01:40:52,740 --> 01:41:08,070
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. You did mention about concealment. So, kailan po masasabi na intentional concealment versus omission yung isang declaration o hindi diniklara o diniklara sa SAL-N na kinita niya ng taong iyon?

413
01:41:08,700 --> 01:41:31,480
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: May mga kaso na decided ang Supreme Court. I just can't remember one of those, the title of those cases now na kung repeated. repeated yung omission that can already demonstrate intentional concealment. Kaya pwedeng maging ground, pwedeng, it can constitute dishonesty.

414
01:41:32,180 --> 01:41:36,020
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. Maraming salamat po, Madam Witness. Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. Thank

415
01:41:36,020 --> 01:41:44,060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you, Senator-Judge Rafi Tulfo. Next, first interjection. Court recognizes Senator-Judge Villanueva. You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed when you're ready.

416
01:41:50,030 --> 01:41:53,980
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. Ma'am, good morning.

417
01:41:57,630 --> 01:42:39,850
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Doon po sa binanggit niyo na pwedeng i-correct ang isang SALN, tingnan po natin yung good faith error versus doon po sa deliberate concealment of wealth. Sa paglalapat po ng prinsipyong ito, Madam Witness, ano pong kongkretong ibidensya ang dapat po nating timbangin? sa inyo pong karanasan para po ma-distinguish talaga itong dalawa na ito and how significant are the officials sa explanation, supporting documents, response to the review and the compliance process ma'am?

418
01:42:40,500 --> 01:42:56,720
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, katulad ng nabanggit ko kanina sir, kapag repeated yan like for five consecutive years Hindi na include yung property niyan. This is a badge na there is an attempt at concealment.

419
01:42:59,020 --> 01:43:00,640
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Pag-repeated. Yes.

420
01:43:00,660 --> 01:43:00,880
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: And

421
01:43:00,880 --> 01:43:09,510
Sen. Joel Villanueva: when you say repeated, ma'am, at least ang repeated, dalawa lang ho yan eh. Pero kung lima, tatlong repeated na ho yan.

422
01:43:12,280 --> 01:43:27,890
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Tama po ba, ma'am? Tama po. And what should be provided to determine po whether or not the correction was made in good faith? or whether the original omission involved deliberate concealment.

423
01:43:28,170 --> 01:43:59,660
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, mayroong isang Supreme Court case actually na in 2002 or 2002 and 2003 na i-declare nung official yung kanya doon sa yung asset na yun sa SAL-N niya but those assets were excluded or not included in his subsequent SAL-Ns. So he was questioned but The Supreme Court said that the Supreme Court found that honest mistake lang yung kanyang nagawa.

424
01:43:59,860 --> 01:44:38,500
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Ma'am, paano niyo po ihiwalay yung dati na niyang pag-aari? For instance, napundar niya habang nasa pwesto po siya. Paano niyo isasaalang-alang kung kailan at... At magkano binili ang mga ito, ang mga utang at ang pagbabago sa halagang nakasaad po sa kanyang sale. Halimbawa po ma'am, kunyari nagbenta po siya ng lupa at ginamit niya yung parehong salapi para bumili ng bahay. How can the court avoid counting the same funds twice when an asset is sold and the proceeds are reinvested?

425
01:44:39,380 --> 01:44:46,960
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Dapat hindi na niya po yung i-include yung naibenta niya, kundi just the proceeds ng kanyang pagbebenta.

426
01:44:48,250 --> 01:45:28,230
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Yung proceeds lang po? Yes. Ma'am, isa pang katanungan. Pinapayagan po ng rules ang pag-grupo ng ilang personal properties. Pero sapat na po bang kasama ang cash sa total ng... Other assets. Madalas ito kasi parang nai-encounter. Kung hindi po malinaw kung magkano ang cash at kung ano ang iba pang ari-arian, kailan po sapat, Madam Witness, ang pag-grupo at kailan naman po kailangan ng hiwalay na detalye?

427
01:45:30,750 --> 01:45:43,800
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: RA 6713, yung cash on hand and cash in bank, they must be specifically declared in the SALN. Hindi pwede i-lump yun sa ibang other personal properties.

428
01:45:44,360 --> 01:45:54,560
Sen. Joel Villanueva: So would you say, ma'am, last na po, Mr. Presiding Officer, would you say that this is not a usual practice? Unusual po na inilalump yung cash dun sa other assets?

429
01:45:56,940 --> 01:46:06,240
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: I will not consider it unusual, but it is against the provision of Section 8 of RA 6713. And

430
01:46:06,240 --> 01:46:12,600
Sen. Joel Villanueva: therefore, if you do that, you are violating the law itself. That's your... Yes

431
01:46:12,600 --> 01:46:45,080
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: sir, pero... Again, doon kasi po sa kaso ni Carlos versus Executive Secretary, meron po tayong tinatawag ng Review and Compliance Procedure under Section 10 of 6713 na binibigyan ng pagkakataon actually yung public official para ayusin kung merong it was not timely filed, it is not in proper form, at saka I just forgot, yung isa pang tatlo po yung kailangan na doon.

432
01:46:46,180 --> 01:46:50,400
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Maraming salamat po, Madam Justice. Thank you. Thank you. Thank

433
01:46:50,660 --> 01:46:58,340
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you, Senator Judge Villanueva. Our Senate President, Senator Wayne Gachalian is recognized for his interjections. You have two minutes, sir.

434
01:46:58,520 --> 01:46:59,000
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Good

435
01:46:59,000 --> 01:47:00,820
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: morning, Madam Justice.

436
01:47:04,770 --> 01:47:05,850
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Unexplained wealth po.

437
01:47:07,710 --> 01:47:27,590
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Sa aking palagay, Hindi naman po yan linalagay sa SAL-N. Typically, hindi nila dinideclare yan kasi unexplained wealth. So, in your opinion, anong mga dokumento ang dapat tignan para po makita at ma-detect po itong unexplained wealth?

438
01:47:30,140 --> 01:48:02,840
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Katulad ng kaso sa Heirs of Ligot versus Sandiganbayan, pati na rin yung sa Rabusa versus Republics. Tinitignan din yung mga assets ng asawa tsaka ng mga anak and even other persons for as long as, according to the case of Ligot versus Sandiganbayan, the acquisition is traceable to the public official.

439
01:48:04,870 --> 01:48:10,190
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Can you cite an example? Paano po matitrace to a public official?

440
01:48:11,570 --> 01:48:44,570
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ang determinant po dyan, ang nagdedetermine yan according to the Supreme Court is, ito bang mga taong ito, yung asawa-anak o yung ibang tao, were they financially capable to lawfully acquire those assets? Kung wala silang kapasidad na bilhin yun in their independent capacity, then that will be traceable yung acquisition na yun doon sa public official. Then that asset will be attributed as asset of the public official.

441
01:48:44,950 --> 01:49:01,090
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Based on your experience, Madam Justice, paano po tinatago ang unexplained wealth? Based on your experience, ano po yung mga nakikita niyong ways para itagoy ng unexplained wealth?

442
01:49:01,470 --> 01:49:15,400
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, yung public official will employ dummies or nominees or even proxies po. Or the assets are registered in the name of or names of other people.

443
01:49:16,750 --> 01:49:20,950
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: How about po yung pag-cash naman po? We're talking about assets.

444
01:49:22,830 --> 01:49:29,650
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Pag cash naman, for example, ayaw niya bumili ng assets but cash, paano pa-detect yung mga ganitong unexplained wealth?

445
01:49:31,380 --> 01:49:52,010
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, kung nasa possession niya yung without depositing it in a bank, mahirap po yun, mahirap yun makita. But if these are deposits in banks and registered in the names of other persons but the ownership

446
01:50:02,110 --> 01:50:02,890
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: How

447
01:50:02,890 --> 01:50:15,210
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: about yung time horizon, Madam Justice? Kailangan gaano kahaba ba yung time horizon na dapat tignan in the accumulation of unexplained wealth?

448
01:50:16,890 --> 01:50:24,440
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Wala namang tinitignan na period po yan. Depende na po yun sa investigation that will be conducted.

449
01:50:28,280 --> 01:50:41,180
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: How about yung unexplained wealth? Pag let's say meron nga nakitang unexplained wealth, sino po ang dapat mag-prove nitong unexplained wealth?

450
01:50:42,400 --> 01:51:17,710
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, katulad ng nasabi ko po kanina, there are three requisites na sinabi ng Supreme Court. para mag-arise itong prima facie presumption of unexplained wealth. Sinabi ng Supreme Court sa kaso ni Heirs of Ligot v. Sandiganbayan, number one, that the respondent is a public officer. Number two, that during his incumbency, he has acquired property that is manifestly disproportionate to his lawful income.

451
01:51:23,880 --> 01:51:30,480
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Assuming yung respondent, dapat ba i-prove niya na this is not unexplained wealth?

452
01:51:31,980 --> 01:51:53,090
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes po. Because this time, because of this prima facie presumption na unlawfully acquired yung property, the burden of proof now shifts to the official to show that he has legitimately acquired those properties alleged to have. alleged to be unlawfully acquired.

453
01:51:53,670 --> 01:52:05,010
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Assuming those are not declared in the SALN, paano niya i-defend o paano niya i-justify yung wealth accumulation?

454
01:52:07,370 --> 01:52:25,510
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, if he can present evidence that he was able to acquire these assets, Lawfully, like from lawful gratuitous gifts

455
01:52:27,210 --> 01:52:31,980
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: or donate gifts. Pwede pa rin yun po.

456
01:52:32,180 --> 01:52:36,680
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Even in the absence of a declaration in the SAL-N, hindi niya din-declare.

457
01:52:39,510 --> 01:52:50,410
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Hindi niya din-declare sa SAL-N niya pero yun ang ginamit niyang defense for his Unexplained wealth. Is that acceptable? Can that be accepted?

458
01:52:51,580 --> 01:52:52,360
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Hindi po.

459
01:52:52,700 --> 01:52:56,620
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: So kailangan ho magtugma sa SAL-N and also the explanation?

460
01:52:57,040 --> 01:52:58,040
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. In

461
01:52:58,040 --> 01:52:58,580
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: other words?

462
01:52:58,860 --> 01:52:59,460
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

463
01:52:59,560 --> 01:53:04,760
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: And pag hindi ho nagtugma, is that grounds for removal or removal from office?

464
01:53:05,900 --> 01:53:09,760
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, according to Section 8

465
01:53:11,360 --> 01:53:13,480
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: of RA No. 3019,

466
01:53:15,320 --> 01:53:32,390
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Kapag napatunayan nga na may unexplained wealth yung tao, yung opisyal, ayon sa pamantayan ng RA 1379, that will serve as a ground for removal or dismissal.

467
01:53:46,160 --> 01:54:19,440
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: This will be quick, Mr. Presiding Officer. Madam Witness, Retired Justice, Paano po pag yung isang opisyal nag-deposit ng 20, 30, o 50 million sa account niya, pero after a few days winidraw niya naman ho? Is that considered ill-gotten or unexplained? Eh winidraw niya naman ho kaagad. Kailangan ba siyang tanungin? Oy, bakit may pera kang ganun? Eh, binidraw niya naman agad. Di naman tumagal sa account. At wala lang. Parang naglaho, parang bula. How's that?

468
01:54:21,640 --> 01:54:37,770
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, siguro ambla nang mag-ano dyan po. Kasi may mga requirements dyan sa Anti-Money Laundering Act regarding itong mga ganitong mga deposits na ito.

469
01:54:38,310 --> 01:55:06,920
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Okay. Paano ko sabihin mo niya, Madam Witness? Hindi naman sa akin yan eh. Hinawakan ko lang para sa iba. For example, sabihin niya sa asawa niya or sa kamag-anak niya, dumaan lang doon, pinahawak lang sa kanya. Pero wala naman, pag three days natin, wala naman talaga, hindi natin makikita doon. Paano naman daw huyo? Kailangan pa ba siyang imbestigahan? Eh sandali lang, three days o one week lang huyong pera doon sa account niya.

470
01:55:07,240 --> 01:55:11,780
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, I will be answering po the question based on

471
01:55:14,200 --> 01:55:32,060
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: 1379. Kung dapat yun dineklara niya sa SAL-N niya at the time na nasa kanya pa. Kung baga, when he filed his SAL-N na nanood pa sa kanyang pangalan yung deposito na yun, ay dapat in-include niya yun sa kanyang assets.

472
01:55:33,080 --> 01:55:51,530
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: So, pero kung within that year, for example, 2026, for example, last month, Pero after few days, winidraw niya kaagad. Winidraw ng opisyal. And wala nang trace. So, ka-questionin pa ba siya? Kailangan pa ba siyang questionin?

473
01:55:52,510 --> 01:56:09,690
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, that will be a different matter. It will not be included in his salin kasi kung at the time he's required to file his salin, wala na yun sa deposito niya sa bangko. But that can be the subject probably of an inquiry by the Anti-Money Laundering Council.

474
01:56:11,290 --> 01:56:13,650
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Thank you Madam Witness. Thank you Presiding Officer.

