Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Thank

521
02:04:36,510 --> 02:04:45,780
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you, Senator Judge Rafi. Senator Judge Kiko Pangilinan, you may proceed, sir, with your interjection. Thank you. Actually,

522
02:04:45,960 --> 02:04:49,520
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: isang question lang. Siguro may isang follow-up kung kailangan.

523
02:04:51,640 --> 02:05:05,440
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Marami kasi ang ating mga kababayan nakikinig, nanonood. Ngayong ill-gotten wealth ang pinag-uusapan. Yung ill-gotten wealth ba kinakailangan pondo ng gobyerno?

524
02:05:06,070 --> 02:05:26,520
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Not necessarily po kasi if you look at the plunder law, there are five overt or criminal acts kung tawagin na if committed through a series or combination at ang na-amass or na-acquire or na-amass na wealth is at the threshold, the minimum threshold of 50 million pesos can still constitute plunder.

525
02:05:27,720 --> 02:05:33,600
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: And the 50 million need not be public funds?

526
02:05:33,960 --> 02:05:47,620
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: No sir, because I think it's paragraph B about bribery. Bribery, the money generally does not come from government but from other persons.

527
02:05:48,360 --> 02:05:51,660
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Okay. Yun lang. Maraming salamat Justice.

528
02:05:52,140 --> 02:05:52,500
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Thank you.

529
02:05:52,500 --> 02:06:15,080
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Before we break for lunch. Just some interjections from the chair. Ma'am, Justice Tang, you said because of the provision on prima facie in 1379, Section 2, the burden of proof shifts? I think you meant the burden of evidence shifts.

530
02:06:15,100 --> 02:06:19,280
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: It's burden of proof, sir, according to the Supreme Court.

531
02:06:19,770 --> 02:06:32,290
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: In Ligot? I didn't see that in Ligot, ma'am. In Ligot, it didn't say that exactly. So the burden, it's your position that the burden of proof and not the burden of evidence shifts?

532
02:06:32,430 --> 02:06:39,190
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. I read that in one case, but I just don't remember the Supreme Court case now.

533
02:06:39,330 --> 02:06:43,550
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: And the basis, if at all, would be Section 2 of 1379?

534
02:06:44,330 --> 02:06:44,950
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

535
02:06:45,930 --> 02:07:04,600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I will respect your opinion, ma'am. I may disagree, but I will respect your opinion. Next. You said upon being asked kung ano yung asset niya at the time of filing. Isn't it asset nung official as of December 31, not at the time of filing? Because filing is on April 30, ma'am.

536
02:07:05,160 --> 02:07:06,480
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. I stand correct.

537
02:07:06,820 --> 02:07:27,060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, as of December 31. Yes, sir. In theory, ma'am, kung may pumasok na pera at lumabas ng October, pumasok at lumabas ng November, pero pagdating ng December 31, wala yun sa account mo. Obligado ka bang i-declare po yun, in your opinion, sa iyong April 30 filing ng SALN?

538
02:07:27,180 --> 02:07:34,420
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: No more, sir, kasi wala na yung asset na yun or pondo at as of December 31 of that year.

539
02:07:34,680 --> 02:07:38,640
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: At doon na po papasok yung binanggit niyong AMLAC? Yes,

540
02:07:38,800 --> 02:07:38,940
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: sir.

541
02:07:39,260 --> 02:07:53,650
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, ma'am. A few more questions, ma'am. You cited Section 6, rather, Article 7 from any source. I asked earlier, you only meant emolument. You didn't meant salary. You didn't meant any other income.

542
02:07:54,090 --> 02:07:57,430
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. Not salary, sir. It's income.

543
02:07:58,990 --> 02:08:00,800
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Kita. So,

544
02:08:00,820 --> 02:08:03,300
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: emolument, you mean, is not limited to salary?

545
02:08:04,900 --> 02:08:08,200
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Shall not receive any emolument. That is salary, sir.

546
02:08:08,480 --> 02:08:09,540
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, salary, ma'am?

547
02:08:09,660 --> 02:08:10,340
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. Yes, sir.

548
02:08:10,440 --> 02:08:22,560
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, let's say may shares of stock. Yung tumakbong presidente, nanalo. Nag-declare ng dividendo yung kumpanya. That's not salary. Is that legal or illegal in your opinion?

549
02:08:23,410 --> 02:08:25,270
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: No, it's not. It's not illegal.

550
02:08:25,850 --> 02:08:28,990
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, he or she can take it? Pwede yan?

551
02:08:29,250 --> 02:08:29,950
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

552
02:08:30,170 --> 02:08:31,470
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kasi hindi siya salary.

553
02:08:32,980 --> 02:09:16,440
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Next, ma'am. Article 7, Section 13 makes mention of the word, participate in any business. My question is, ba't hindi sinabi sa Saligang Batas, have an interest in any business? Bakit participate? Kasi nakalagay sa bandang huling ng provision ng Section 13, conflict of interest. Ito hindi sinasabing conflict of interest. Binanggit lang yung conflict of interest in relation to a contract with government or a financial interest with any license or franchise issued by government. Pero nilagay po sa business, participate in business. Ano po ibig sabihin? Hindi siya pwedeng magmay-ari ng negosyo o hindi siya pwedeng makilahok sa negosyong pag-ari niya. Meaning actively run it.

554
02:09:18,830 --> 02:09:22,910
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Your Honor, ang participate naman nakalagay dyan directly or indirectly.

555
02:09:25,230 --> 02:09:25,870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Meaning?

556
02:09:26,190 --> 02:09:39,280
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Meaning, whether ownership in a corporation or participating either as a director or as an officer of the corporation, that is prohibited.

557
02:09:39,880 --> 02:10:01,510
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ma'am, it is in line, directly or indirectly is in line with the practice of any other profession, participate in any business. Hindi ba parang ibig sabihin ito? Kapag ka pangulo kay kalawang pangulo, huwag mong pagkaabalahan ano pang ibang bagay. Ito ang pangunahin mong trabaho. Ito lang ang dapat mong tutukan. Yes, sir. Does it also include not owning a business?

558
02:10:02,390 --> 02:10:03,150
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

559
02:10:03,780 --> 02:10:14,730
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, it is your position that a president and or vice president should divest from any businesses that they may have after they take their oath?

560
02:10:15,190 --> 02:10:25,550
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. In fact, there is... Under the law, there is a need to divest upon assumption of office immediately and within 30 days.

561
02:10:27,160 --> 02:10:28,540
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: What law would that be, ma'am?

562
02:10:29,080 --> 02:10:31,780
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: I think it's 6713, sir.

563
02:10:32,420 --> 02:10:34,300
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: It's in the Code of Ethical Standards?

564
02:10:34,560 --> 02:10:34,720
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes.

565
02:10:35,370 --> 02:10:43,250
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I see that being done by most secretaries whenever they're appointed, whenever they have a business that's related to the department they will be heading,

566
02:10:43,470 --> 02:10:44,150
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: as

567
02:10:44,150 --> 02:10:54,690
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: we have seen in the past. So it is your position that if you are President and Vice President, you have to divest from any and all businesses. Mas kinasari-sari store pa yan?

568
02:10:54,690 --> 02:10:55,650
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

569
02:10:55,650 --> 02:10:56,810
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: That is your position, ma'am?

570
02:10:56,910 --> 02:10:57,410
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

571
02:10:57,470 --> 02:11:07,550
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: And finally, ma'am, on SAL-N, pare-pareho lang po naman ng SAL-N ng Presidente, Vice, at ng bawat opisyal ng pamahalaan, di po ba?

572
02:11:08,280 --> 02:11:12,520
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. Because there is a prescribed form by the Civil Service Commission.

573
02:11:13,080 --> 02:11:26,580
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Then why does the prescribed form mention business interest if it's prohibited from a president and vice president? It's the same form they fill up, ma'am. Why does it still include a blank for business interest if it's prohibited?

574
02:11:28,200 --> 02:11:35,060
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, it's a pro-form. It's a form that is prepared by the Civil Service Commission.

575
02:11:37,550 --> 02:11:46,320
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: All that the public, the president or vice president as the case may be, will do is to state they're not applicable, sir.

576
02:11:46,600 --> 02:12:00,800
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Or umaasaan sa civil service na malay mo, madulas, magkamali, umamin. Meaning, there are only two officials, ma'am, president and vice president. I'm sure they can come up with a form for them specially. Wouldn't you think so? If at all for the future, if not now?

577
02:12:01,520 --> 02:12:02,240
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

578
02:12:02,940 --> 02:12:05,620
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Perhaps, right? Because it's there. The blank is there to be filled up.

579
02:12:06,780 --> 02:12:07,320
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

580
02:12:07,660 --> 02:12:10,100
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So ang ilalagay dapat na nun, ma'am, not applicable?

581
02:12:10,620 --> 02:12:11,240
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

582
02:12:11,400 --> 02:12:13,300
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: If you're president and vice president?

583
02:12:13,560 --> 02:12:14,040
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir.

584
02:12:14,540 --> 02:12:22,770
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: That would be all, Madam Justice. Senator-Judge Pia, Senator-Judge J.V. Ejercito, and then we break for lunch?

585
02:12:22,770 --> 02:12:26,290
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: I thought there were no other senator-judges, that's why I already interjected.

586
02:12:26,290 --> 02:12:27,270
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, Senator-Judge Pia.

587
02:12:27,270 --> 02:12:28,430
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: No, actually, mine

588
02:12:28,430 --> 02:12:31,090
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: is just a follow-up to his Honor's question.

589
02:12:32,750 --> 02:13:25,350
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Good afternoon, Justice. Good afternoon. Just a clarification on your response to the presiding officer. His earlier question was about the need to, if in your opinion, the president or vice president can hold on to stocks and receive dividends. And your answer was yes, they can receive dividends. You answered that earlier, hindi ba? Mr. Presiding Officer, can you confirm? She answered yes. Can I say something? Sure. I'll complete my question because precisely I want it clarified. And then in his succeeding question where we talked about divesting, sabi niyo they have to divest. So what would now be the difference between your first answer and your second answer? Because holding of stocks is also a form of ownership.

590
02:13:26,140 --> 02:13:43,100
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, regarding the receipt of dividends, if those dividends already accrued before assumption of office, then that becomes divested right of the stockholder. There

591
02:13:43,100 --> 02:13:43,940
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: is

592
02:13:43,940 --> 02:13:45,820
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: no legal prohibition to that.

593
02:13:46,140 --> 02:14:04,930
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: So ma'am, are you now clarifying your answer that If it was accrued prior to the assumption of office, then they may receive it, but upon assumption of office, they should be divesting of all kinds of investment, all stock ownerships.

594
02:14:05,070 --> 02:14:05,770
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, ma'am.

595
02:14:06,050 --> 02:14:21,810
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: So it doesn't matter if it is publicly listed, that you have no say, that you have shares that are just sitting there. Wala nang pinagkaiba yun sa closed corporations with limited stockholders. There's no difference in your opinion.

596
02:14:22,130 --> 02:14:22,690
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, ma'am.

597
02:14:22,710 --> 02:14:31,050
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: So that's very different from my understanding of the earlier response that you gave. But thank you for clarifying that. Thank you,

598
02:14:31,070 --> 02:14:31,210
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: ma

599
02:14:31,210 --> 02:14:31,310
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: 'am.

600
02:14:31,810 --> 02:14:35,050
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator-Judge JV is recognized. Then we pause for lunch.

601
02:14:36,010 --> 02:14:38,490
Sen. Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Mr. President. Good morning, Justice.

602
02:14:39,660 --> 02:14:40,400
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Good morning, sir.

603
02:14:40,580 --> 02:14:55,920
Sen. Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Justice, is it correct to say that the unexplained wealth is automatically illegally accumulated wealth or it does not follow? Ibig mo ba sabihin na ito ay, kung hindi na ipaliwanag ka agad, ay ito ay illegal ka agad o galing nakaw?

604
02:14:56,660 --> 02:15:15,040
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, according to Republic Act 1379, sir, may opportunity yung official to explain kung merong manifest disproportionality from his lawful income at sa kanyang pagmamayari, yung kanyang yaman.

605
02:15:16,720 --> 02:15:39,580
Sen. Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pangano po Justice, in your judicial experience, have you encountered instances when unexplained wealth was sufficiently explained by the public official? So sa inyo pong experience, may mga kaso ko ba na mukhang unexplained wealth sa umpisa pero Kalaunan ay ito'y napatunayan na hindi na mapalawag galing sa illegal o nakao.

606
02:15:41,190 --> 02:15:43,010
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: No, sir. Wala po.

607
02:15:46,390 --> 02:15:59,340
Sen. Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Just a few points, Mr. President. Is it important for unexplained wealth to be acquired during the incumbency? So yung questionable yaman o ari-arian na nakuha mismo ay habang dapat nananungkulan ang public official?

608
02:15:59,660 --> 02:16:29,930
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, sir. According to the Supreme Court, again, in the case of heirs of Ligot versus Sandiganbayan kasi tatlo ang requisites niyan before this presumption may apply. Dapat siya ay public officer and then naka-accumulate siya ng vast wealth. During his incumbency. And third, he cannot satisfactorily explain kung paano niya nakuha yung yaman na yun. Lawfully.

609
02:16:30,740 --> 02:16:47,040
Sen. Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Last point, Sir President. What if the unexplained wealth is not acquired during the incumbency of the public official but before he assumed office? Kumbaga kung na-acquired niyo ito bago siya nag-anongkulan o nag-assume? As an official.

610
02:16:47,420 --> 02:17:09,120
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: If he acquired those money, that money unlawfully as a private individual, ibang usapan na po yun. He cannot be sued because of his incumbency dyan.

611
02:17:10,330 --> 02:17:11,810
Sen. Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Sir. Thank

612
02:17:12,580 --> 02:17:31,330
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you. With the permission of Senator Judge Riza, can we do her interjections after lunch and or after the cross of Attorney Mark? The time is 12.11. We shall resume at 12.45.

613
02:17:33,900 --> 02:17:35,860
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: We shall

614
02:17:37,300 --> 02:17:38,360
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: resume at 1 o'clock.

615
02:17:46,320 --> 02:17:50,600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Trial is suspended. We are on recess until 1pm. Thank you.

616
03:07:57,140 --> 03:08:06,500
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly situate Justice Cabotaje Tang at the witness stand. Kindly assist her, please.

617
03:08:24,390 --> 03:08:26,810
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ma'am, nakakain po kayo, Justice Tang?

618
03:08:27,780 --> 03:08:28,700
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes, Your Honor.

619
03:08:29,060 --> 03:08:44,310
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You shall continue with your testimony under the same oath. Attorney Mark, do you want to do your cross first or do you want to allow... Senator Riza, for her interjection.

620
03:08:44,880 --> 03:08:46,220
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: We can allow her first.

621
03:08:46,600 --> 03:08:49,860
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You're both giving way, so I will listen to her. She says

622
03:08:49,860 --> 03:08:51,000
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: kayo...

623
03:08:52,830 --> 03:08:54,410
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator-Judge Risa, you want to proceed?

624
03:08:56,550 --> 03:08:58,610
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Riza, you want to proceed?

625
03:08:58,610 --> 03:08:59,430
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Yes.

626
03:08:59,430 --> 03:09:04,090
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed with your interjection before we proceed with the cross of the respondent.

627
03:09:08,920 --> 03:09:10,400
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

628
03:09:12,900 --> 03:09:26,540
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat sa defense, although I was willing to listen to their crosswords. In any case po, Mr. Presiding Officer, magandang hapon po, Justice. Good afternoon, ma'am. Good afternoon po. Ilang mga tanong na lamang po.

629
03:09:28,830 --> 03:09:35,830
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So nabanggit niyo po kanina na may prima facie presumption sa mga kaso ng unexplained wealth.

630
03:09:37,460 --> 03:09:42,700
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Kailan po pumapasok o kailan nagkikick in yung ganyang presumption?

631
03:09:45,000 --> 03:10:12,260
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Katulad po nang nabanggit ko kanina, according to the Supreme Court, in the case of heirs of Ligot versus Sandigan Bayan, tatlo po ang requisites niyan bago mag-apply yung presumption. Number one, the respondent is a public officer. Number two, he acquired properties during his incumbency that are gross. Number three, these properties are grossly disproportionate to his salary,

632
03:10:13,780 --> 03:10:18,980
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: lawful income, or sources from other legitimately acquired property.

633
03:10:20,870 --> 03:10:25,130
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So, bakit po gumawa ng ganyang presumption yung batas?

634
03:10:25,450 --> 03:10:26,110
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: To

635
03:10:29,600 --> 03:10:35,830
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: make it easier, I believe, for the government to go after errant public officials.

636
03:10:37,980 --> 03:10:58,260
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: And yet, sabi niyo rin po kanina na historically in the preceding years, In fact, naging mas mahirap para sa prosecution ang mag-prosecute ng mga kaso ng plunder. At sabi niyo pa po kanina, baka nga dapat i-review ng Kongreso ang mga kaukulang batas.

637
03:10:58,860 --> 03:11:00,800
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: That's my personal opinion, ma'am.

638
03:11:00,900 --> 03:11:24,000
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Opo. Alright. Salamat po. Sabi niyo rin po kanina, magkakaiba yung hidden wealth, ill-gotten wealth, at saka unexplained wealth. Tama po ba na sa mga kaso ng unexplained wealth sa mga public officials, hindi po kailangang patunayan na galing sa illegal o ill-gotten ang yaman?

639
03:11:24,740 --> 03:11:35,260
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Ang sabi ng batas po ay unlawfully acquired yung property. Meaning to say, these assets were acquired laban or labag sa batas.

640
03:11:36,370 --> 03:11:37,090
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Okay.

641
03:11:40,650 --> 03:11:44,390
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So, kailangan patunayan in that case?

642
03:11:45,520 --> 03:11:58,860
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Yes ma'am. But again, there is that presumption na kapag yung three requisites na nabanggit ko ay present, there is that presumption of that these properties were acquired illegally.

643
03:11:59,180 --> 03:11:59,880
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Yes

644
03:11:59,880 --> 03:12:00,300
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: ma'am.

645
03:12:00,300 --> 03:12:09,800
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So ang kailangan lamang ay mapakita na may malaking kayamanan na hindi maipaliwanag saan galing. Yes ma'am.

646
03:12:12,820 --> 03:12:15,860
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Marami salamat po, Justice. Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

647
03:12:15,940 --> 03:12:20,160
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator-Judge Hontiveros. Are you ready for your cross, Attorney Mark?

648
03:12:20,480 --> 03:12:20,960
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yes, Your Honor.

649
03:12:21,680 --> 03:12:23,460
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed, sir, when you're ready.

650
03:12:24,040 --> 03:12:28,720
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, we are conducting cross-examination ad cautelam, for the record, Your Honor.

651
03:12:30,800 --> 03:12:32,700
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, given your continuing objection.

652
03:12:34,360 --> 03:12:35,420
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Good afternoon, Justice.

653
03:12:35,820 --> 03:12:36,560
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Good afternoon, sir.

654
03:12:38,020 --> 03:12:42,700
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: You served in government for over 40 years, correct? Around 40 years.

655
03:12:43,960 --> 03:12:44,720
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: 44 years.

656
03:12:45,220 --> 03:12:49,820
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Before anything else, thank you po for your many years of service in government. Thank

657
03:12:49,820 --> 03:12:49,880
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: you.

