Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Pia Cayetano, again to avail of round two before Senator Erwin's round three. You have two minutes, ma'am.

1393
04:39:20,970 --> 04:39:48,760
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you. I'd also like to express my gratitude to the justice, not just for appearing today, but for your years of service. Talagang your whole career was dedicated. Thank you for that. And then fun fact for everyone, the writ of amparo was a question in my bar examinations. And at that time... I think it was only mentioned one in some very old case so I think yung Bartop-Natcher lang yata yung nakasagot ng question na yun. And thanks to the...

1394
04:39:50,780 --> 04:40:20,210
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: The inclusion, then now everybody knows, well at least every lawyer knows what the rate of comparison, but believe me, none of us knew and I thought I failed the bar because of that question. On that note, I have a very simple follow-up question. Ako naman wala akong balak magtanong but my colleagues asked very interesting questions regarding impartial trial. What about, ma'am, threats, intimidations, and pressures to judges? Are those allowed to have an impartial tribunal?

1395
04:40:20,870 --> 04:40:22,190
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: No, ma'am.

1396
04:40:22,910 --> 04:40:39,510
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Have you ever encountered anything, not you personally, but situations similar to that that judges, whether in Sandigan or because of your profession, have received in public such threats and intimidations?

1397
04:40:40,550 --> 04:40:46,910
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: No, ma'am. Not in relation to pending cases before the Sandigan buy-in. I'm happy

1398
04:40:46,910 --> 04:40:48,770
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: for you kasi kami ho meron. Thank you.

1399
04:40:49,610 --> 04:41:06,850
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I think the Rito Famparo question in the bar was counted in favor of all the examinees at that time, if I remember correctly, Senator-Judge Pia. Ito sa bonus point already, given the difficulty of the question asked, if I remember correctly. Senator-Judge Irwin, tool for his recognition.

1400
04:41:12,630 --> 04:41:21,010
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: One last quick question, Madam Witness. Based on your experience as a judge po, hukom,

1401
04:41:24,530 --> 04:41:58,440
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Magistrado, can you make a ruling on a case presented before you or in your court by simply listening to the testimonies or testimony of a witness and the questions by the counsels? Can you make a ruling and say na? Okay, this person is guilty or not? That's not possible or is it possible?

1402
04:41:59,530 --> 04:42:08,770
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Well, if the testimonial evidence is credible and a judgment can be rendered on the basis thereof, that can suffice, sir.

1403
04:42:08,970 --> 04:42:21,560
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: But you might still need documentations, right ma'am? Or you just merely, or will you wait for documents to prove na there's a case by the prosecution or by the defense?

1404
04:42:22,860 --> 04:42:30,720
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Sir, that will depend on whether there is a need for presentation of documentary evidence because evidence is either testimonial or documentary.

1405
04:42:31,140 --> 04:42:49,220
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Exactly, but what I mean to say is like documents, ma'am. Documentations. Or sapat na ang testimonya para to say na conclude na itong... Taon na ito ay guilty or you might still need as a judge ika nga ng documents to be presented before the court?

1406
04:42:49,400 --> 04:42:54,560
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: Sir, that would really depend on the nature of the case presented before the court.

1407
04:42:55,970 --> 04:42:58,590
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Alright, thank you po Madam Witness. Thank you

1408
04:42:58,590 --> 04:42:58,750
Justice Amparo M. Cabotaje-Tang: sir.

1409
04:43:00,530 --> 04:43:26,300
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: There being no other Senator-Judge who wishes to make interventions, Justice Tang, maraming salamat po sa inyong panahon, sa inyong oras, sa inyong pasensya. At sa inyong pagsagot sa mga katanungan mula sa magkabilang panig ng impeachment complaint na nakabimbin ngayon sa Senado bilang isang impeachment court. Maraming salamat po at magandang hapon sa inyo ma'am. Thank you for your cooperation and thank you ma'am for your service. You were excused ma'am.

1410
04:43:35,630 --> 04:43:40,710
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Just some administrative matters. According to the Senate President, we'll call session at 3.15.

1411
04:43:44,230 --> 04:44:19,540
